  "challenge": {
    "title": "Meeting Family Over a Meal",
    "instructions": "Write and say a short Gulf Arabic conversation that lasts at least 10 lines. It must include a question about someone's family, a description of at least one relative, a statement of hunger or thirst, ordering or offering food and drink, the fixed exchange بالعافية / الله يعافيك or صحة وعافية / الله يعافيك, and asking for the bill. Use at least 8 target phrases from Unit 2 and include both a masculine-address form and a feminine-address form.",
    "required_elements": [
      "A question about family using عندك عايلة كبيرة؟ or كم عددكم في العايلة؟",
      "A description of at least one family member using أمي, أبوي, خوي, ختي, زوجي, مرتي, ولدي, or بنتي.",
      "A statement of hunger or thirst using جوعان, جوعانة, or عطشان.",
      "An order or offer of food or drink using أبي آكل or أبي أشرب.",
      "The fixed exchange بالعافية / الله يعافيك, or صحة وعافية / الله يعافيك.",
      "A request for the bill using الحساب لو سمحت or كم الحساب؟",
      "Both a masculine-address form (such as عندك) and a feminine-address form (such as عندچ)."
    ],
